<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Black Rangers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1772">1772</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Redi Musu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Black Rangers were a corps of formerly enslaved men raised by the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> in 1772 to fight maroon groups, especially those led by Boni, in return for their freedom. Known from their red caps as the Redi Musu, they knew the forest well and proved more effective than European troops, serving alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> soldiers described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-gabriel-stedman">John Gabriel Stedman</a>.</p></div>
